pistomp-usb-automount (1.0.0-2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Mount via a udev-activated systemd unit: udevd's SystemCallFilter
    blocks mount(2) with EPERM in RUN programs, and PrivateMounts hides
    any mount that did succeed.
  * Fix unmount on unplug. The blkid filesystem guard ran before the action
    switch, so removal — where the device node is already gone — always
    exited early and left a stale mount. The mountpoint now comes from
    /proc/mounts, which also survives labels blkid can no longer report.
  * Log mount failures instead of silently removing the mountpoint.

 -- Cam Gorrie <sastraxi@gmail.com>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 22:40:15 +0000

pistomp-usb-automount (1.0.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Extracted from stage2/01-sys-tweaks so the fix reaches
    already-deployed devices via OTA, not just new images.

